WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------
Runsheet r2 §3.7 told the operator to "apply the separately reviewed
mechanical fixation/activation delta" and then, in step 6, to run
tests.test_receipt_histsem. No such delta was ever authored, and the step
that needed it was sequenced AFTER the suite run. Both defects are cured
here: the delta is a real reviewed artifact with a digest in the candidate
manifest, and r3 §3.7 applies it BEFORE the suite runs.

DESIGN CHOICE — WHAT IS A LITERAL AND WHAT IS DERIVED
-----------------------------------------------------
Exactly ONE value in this delta is substituted at the bench:
SUCCESSOR_PINSET_SHA256. It has to be a literal, and it cannot be a
derivation, because it is the BYTE AUTHENTICATOR for the successor
allowlist class (runsheet §4(e), row "successor pinset JSON"). A test that
derived the digest from the file it is checking would recompute to whatever
a tampered file now hashes to and would authenticate nothing. The digest is
unknowable before the mint, so the delta ships an obviously-invalid
sentinel, "S0-FIXATION-SUBSTITUTION-PENDING", and r3 §3.7 step 5
substitutes it mechanically from the minted bytes. The sentinel is not 64
hex characters on purpose: an unsubstituted delta fails loudly on the guard
assertion rather than silently pinning a plausible-looking value (a
64-zero placeholder would not have that property).

Everything else is either a REVIEWED LITERAL or a DERIVATION:

  * SUCCESSOR_PACK_COUNT (3) and SUCCESSOR_RECEIPT_COUNT (33) are ruled
    before the mint by D-151, so they are reviewed literals in this file --
    not bench substitutions.
  * The v1 member's literals (PINSET_SHA256, 9 packs, 99 receipts, 108
    facts) are UNTOUCHED, exactly as D-151 condition 3 requires; the delta
    only re-scopes them so they state what they always meant -- the v1
    member's own coordinates -- instead of standing in for whole-corpus
    totals that stop being true the moment the successor is minted.
  * The whole-corpus totals in
    test_full_corpus_verifies_two_coordinates_and_facts now DERIVE from the
    loaded chain (9 rows before the mint, 12 after). They are consistency
    checks, not authenticators. Substituting 12/132/<new fact count> as
    literals would have added three more unreviewable bench edits while
    authenticating nothing that the two per-member digest pins do not
    already authenticate.
  * test_differential_self_test_all_nine_packs is renamed to
    test_differential_self_test_all_governed_packs and iterates the loaded
    chain. r2 called the old name "then-false"; iterating the chain makes
    the method true in BOTH coordinates with no bench edit.

WHAT AN INDEPENDENT REVIEWER RECOMPUTES (r3 §3.7 step 7)
--------------------------------------------------------
sha256 of $CLONE/configs/arm_readiness/legacy_receipt_histsem_pinset_v4_v1.json
at the fixation commit; that it equals the substituted SUCCESSOR_PINSET_SHA256;
that it equals table.successor_pinset.sha256 in Ed's confirmed step-6 table;
and that the successor's pack/receipt counts are 3 and 33.

